From b1f611bc3b0943bdd182f501ce5e7ff0ec48235d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:10:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: a 410 on a primary board's live file
 sweeps this gateway's rows the snapshot lacks

When the live pull of a primary board raised Resync, sync_board resynced the live file in place
(partition=gateway). A snapshot carries only live rows and resync only upserts, so a row of this
gateway's cards that the Board deleted below its retention floor stayed in the live file forever.
The replica path is safe (it unlinks and rebuilds its file); the live file cannot be unlinked: it
holds unpushed local cards, local tombstones and picked-up copies of other gateways' cards.

New hermes_cli/kanban_sync_resync_sweep.py: resync_live() runs the same resync through a hub proxy
that records each snapshot table's uids, then sweep_absent() deletes only rows that are
- in this gateway's partition: a card created_on this gateway (or unset), a link whose child is
  such a card, a child row of such a card (picked-up foreign copies are never swept);
- absent from a snapshot table read to its last page (an aborted resync sweeps nothing);
- not held locally: no outbox op for the row (pending or rejected) or for its card, no tombstone;
- not created after the rebuild began; task_events older than the Board's event retention are
  kept (the Board drops those without a delete).
The deletes go through apply_remote_changes (feed delete handlers, tombstones, observers),
children before cards. apply_remote_changes gains keep=, asked about each change inside its
transaction, so every candidate is re-checked atomically with its delete. sync_board already
holds board_sync_lock for the round.

Dormant: no Board has advanced a retention floor yet. Follow-up of t_01a1d5d6e37eafd6 (the
install-boards replica sweep in state); card t_01a1d5f9de4020fa.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_live_resync_sweep.py. The round test pushes two own
cards and two comments, has the Board delete one card and one comment, advances the floor, then
runs a round with /ops down (a new local card stays pending) and a picked-up foreign copy in the
file. RED on main at `assert gone not in tasks`; GREEN with the fix: the deleted card and comment
are gone (with tombstones), the kept card, its kept comment, the unpushed local card (outbox
still pending) and the foreign copy remain, cursor at the head. Two unit tests cover the
rejected-outbox, tombstone, written-after-start and incomplete-snapshot guards.
